itle=Ben+Kovitz&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fc2.com%2Fcgi%2Fwiki%3FBenKovitz&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+Wikipedia" class=Z3988 about=#mwt78 id=mwDU8></span> – see also Ben Kovitz' fuller account which he links from there.</span></li>
<li about=#cite_note-Glyn_Moody-24 id=cite_note-Glyn_Moody-24 data-mw-footnote-number=24><span rel=mw:referencedBy class=mw-cite-backlink id=mwDVA><a href=#cite_ref-Glyn_Moody_24-0 id=mwDVE><span class=cite-accessibility-label>Jump up to: </span><span class="mw-linkback-text sf-hidden" id=mwDVI>1</span></a> <a href=#cite_ref-Glyn_Moody_24-1 id=mwDVM><span class="mw-linkback-text sf-hidden" id=mwDVQ>2</span></a></span> <span id=mw-reference-text-cite_note-Glyn_Moody-24 class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel=mw-deduplicated-inline-style href=mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106 about=#mwt81 typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id=mwDVU data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Cite news &quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cite_news&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;last&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Moody&quot;},&quot;first&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Glyn&quot;},&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;13 July 2006&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;This time, it'll be a Wikipedia written by experts&quot;},&quot;work&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;The Guardian&quot;},&quot;location&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;London&quot;},&quot;url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2006/jul/13/media.newmedia&quot;},&quot;url-status&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;live&quot;},&quot;access-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;25 March 2007&quot;},&quot;archive-url&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;https://web.archive.org/web/20070222023201/http://technology.guardian.co.uk/weekly/story/0,,1818630,00.html&quot;},&quot;archive-date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;22 February 2007&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><cite id=CITEREFMoody2006 class="citation news cs1" about=#mwt81>Moody, Glyn (July 13, 2006). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href=https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2006/jul/13/media.newmedia class="external text" id=mwDVY>"This time, it'll be a Wikipedia written by experts"</a>. <i id=mwDVc>The Guardian</i>. London. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href=https://web.archive.org/web/20070222023201/http://technology.guardian.co.uk/weekly/story/0,,1818630,00.html class="external text" id=mwDVg>Archived</a> from the original on February 22, 2007<span class=reference-accessdate id=mwDVk>. Retrieved <span class=nowrap id=mwDVo>March 25,</span> 2007</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Guardian&amp;rft.atitle=This+time%2C+it%27ll+be+a+Wikipedia+written+by+experts&amp;rft.date=2006-07-13&amp;rft.aulast=Moody&amp;rft.aufirst=Glyn&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Ftechnology%2F2006%2Fjul%2F13%2Fmedia.newmedia&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+Wikipedia" class=Z3988 about=#mwt81 id=mwDVs></span> – While casting around for a way to speed up article production, Sanger met with Kovitz, an old friend, in January 2001. Kovitz introduced Sanger to the idea of the wiki, invented in 1995 by Ward Cunningham: web pages that anyone could write and edit. "My first reaction was that this really could be what would solve the problem," Sanger explains, "because the software was already written, and this community of people on WikiWikiWeb" – the first wiki – "had created something like 14,000 pages". Nupedia, by contrast, had produced barely two dozen articles. Sanger took up the idea immediately: "I wrote up a proposal and sent it [to Wales] that evening, and the wiki was then set up for me to work on." But this was not Wikipedia as we know it. "Originally it was the Nupedia Wiki – our idea was to use it as an article incubator for Nupedia. Articles could begin life on this wiki, be developed collaboratively and, when they got to a certain stage of development, be put into the Nupedia system."</span></li>
<li about=#cite_note-Origins_of_Wikipedia-25 id=cite_note-Origins_of_Wikipedia-25 data-mw-footnote-number=25><span rel=mw:referencedBy class=mw-cite-backlink id=mwDVw><a href=#cite_ref-Origins_of_Wikipedia_25-0 id=mwDV0><span class=cite-accessibility-label>Jump up to: </span><span class="mw-linkback-text sf-hidden" id=mwDV4>1</span></a> <a href=#cite_ref-Origins_of_Wikipedia_25-1 id=mwDV8><span class="mw-linkback-text sf-hidden" id=mwDWA>2</span></a></span> <span id=mw-reference-text-cite_note-Origins_of_Wikipedia-25 class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel=mw-deduplicated-inline-style href=mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106 about=#mwt84 typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id=mwDWE data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Sidener"},"first":{"wt":"Jonathan"},"date":{"wt":"23 September 2006"},"title":{"wt":"Wikipedia co-founder looks to add accountability, end anarchy"},"work":{"wt":"[[The San Diego Union-Tribune]]"},"url":{"wt":"http://www.signonsandiego.com/uniontrib/20060923/news_lz1n23wiki.html"},"url-status":{"wt":"dead"},"access-date":{"wt":"25 March 2007"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20071017041126/http://www.signonsandiego.com/uniontrib/20060923/news_lz1n23wiki.html"},"archive-date":{"wt":"17 October 2007"},"quote":{"wt":"The origins of Wikipedia date to 2000, when Sanger was finishing his doctoral thesis in philosophy and had an idea for a Web site."}},"i":0}}]}'><cite id=CITEREFSidener2006 class="citation news cs1" about=#mwt84>Sidener, Jonathan (September 23, 2006). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href=https://web.archive.org/web/20071017041126/http://www.signonsandiego.com/uniontrib/20060923/news_lz1n23wiki.html class="external text" id=mwDWI>"Wikipedia co-founder looks to add accountability, end anarchy"</a>. <i id=mwDWM><a rel=mw:WikiLink href=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_San_Diego_Union-Tribune title="The San Diego Union-Tribune" id=mwDWQ>The San Diego Union-Tribune</a></i>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href=http://www.signonsandiego.com/uniontrib/20060923/news_lz1n23wiki.html class="external text" id=mwDWU>the original</a> on October 17, 2007<span class=reference-accessdate id=mwDWY>. Retrieved <span class=nowrap id=mwDWc>March 25,</span> 2007</span>. <q id=mwDWg>The origins of Wikipedia date to 2000, when Sanger was finishing his doctoral thesis in philosophy and had an idea for a Web site.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+San+Diego+Union-Tribune&amp;rft.atitle=Wikipedia+co-founder+looks+to+add+accountability%2C+end+anarchy&amp;rft.date=2006-09-23&amp;rft.aulast=Sidener&amp;rft.aufirst=Jonathan&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.signonsandiego.com%2Funiontrib%2F20060923%2Fnews_lz1n23wiki.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+Wikipedia" class=Z3988 about=#mwt84 id=mwDWk></span></span></li>
<li about=#cite_note-the_hive-26 id=cite_note-the_hive-26 data-mw-footnote-number=26><span class=mw-cite-backlink id=mwDWo><a href=#cite_ref-the_hive_26-0 rel=mw:referencedBy id=mwDWs aria-label="Jump up" title="Jump up"><span class="mw-linkback-text sf-hidden" id=mwDWw>↑</span></a></span> <span id=mw-reference-text-cite_note-the_hive-26 class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel=mw-deduplicated-inline-style href=mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106 about=#mwt91 typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id=mwDW0 data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite magazine ","href":"./Template:Cite_magazine"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Poe"},"first":{"wt":"Marshall"},"date":{"wt":"September 2006"},"title":{"wt":"The Hive"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.theatlantic.com/doc/200609/wikipedia/3"},"url-status":{"wt":"live"},"magazine":{"wt":"[[The Atlantic Monthly]]"},"page":{"wt":"3"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20061110160718/http://www.theatlantic.com/doc/200609/wikipedia/3"},"archive-date":{"wt":"10 November 2006"},"access-date":{"wt":"25 March 2007"}},"i":0}}]}'><cite id=mwDW4 class="citation magazine cs1" about=#mwt91 data-x-id=CITEREFPoe2006>Poe, Marshall (September 2006). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href=https://www.theatlantic.com/doc/200609/wikipedia/3 class="external text" id=mwDW8>"The Hive"</a>. <i id=mwDXA><a rel=mw:WikiLink href=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Atlantic_Monthly title="The Atlantic Monthly" class=mw-redirect id=mwDXE>The Atlantic Monthly</a></i>. p.<span typeof=mw:Entity id=mwDXI>&nbsp;</span>3. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href=https://web.archive.org/web/20061110160718/http://www.theatlantic.com/doc/200609/wikipedia/3 class="external text" id=mwDXM>Archived</a> from the original on November 10, 2006<span class=reference-accessdate id=mwDXQ>. Retrieved <span class=nowrap id=mwDXU>March 25,</span> 2007</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Atlantic+Monthly&amp;rft.atitle=The+Hive&amp;rft.pages=3&amp;rft.date=2006-09&amp;rft.aulast=Poe&amp;rft.aufirst=Marshall&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theatlantic.com%2Fdoc%2F200609%2Fwikipedia%2F3&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+Wikipedia" class=Z3988 about=#mwt91 id=mwDXY></span> – "Over tacos that night, Sanger explained his concerns about Nupedia's lack of progress, the root cause of which was its serial editorial system. As Nupedia was then structured, no stage of the editorial process could proceed before the previous stage was completed. Kovitz brought up the wiki and sketched out 'wiki magic,' the mysterious process by which communities with common interests work to improve wiki pages by incremental contributions. If it worked for the rambunctious hacker culture of programming, Kovitz said, it could work for any online collaborative project. The wiki could break the Nupedia bottleneck by permitting volunteers to work simultaneously all over the project. With Kovitz in tow, Sanger rushed back to his apartment and called Wales to share the idea. Over the next few days, he wrote a formal proposal for Wales and started a page on Cunningham's wiki called 'Wikipedia.<span style=padding-right:0.15em about=#mwt93 typeof=mw:Transclusion id=mwDXc data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'-&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:'-&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span typeof=mw:Entity id=mwDXg>'</span></span>"</span></li>
