pan>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Wired+News&amp;rft.atitle=Assignment+Zero+First+Take%3A+Wiki+Innovators+Rethink+Openness&amp;rft.date=2007-05-03&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.wired.com%2Ftechbiz%2Fmedia%2Fnews%2F2007%2F05%2Fassignment_zero_citizendium&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHistory+of+Wikipedia" class=Z3988 about=#mwt98 id=mwDZA></span> Wired.com states: "Wales offered the following on-the-record comment in an e-mail to NewAssignment.net editor [and NYU Professor] <a rel=mw:WikiLink href=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay_Rosen title="Jay Rosen" id=mwDZE>Jay Rosen</a> ...' Larry Sanger was my employee working under my direct supervision during the entire process of launching Wikipedia. He was not the originator of the proposal to use a wiki for the encyclopedia project – that was Jeremy Rosenfeld'."</span></li>
